From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/adreno: match removal to the probe registration mode

An unbound component has no master private data. Reading kms_init from that
pointer faults while unloading MSM on a firmware-framebuffer system. Select
component deletion or the independent GPU removal using the same condition as
probe, including the Imageon path. Keep component and GPU lifetime paired.

Observed on Uke with Linux 7.2.10, no native display master and default
separate_gpu_kms=0; adreno_remove faults on a NULL private pointer.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c
@@ -280,12 +280,11 @@
 
 static void adreno_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
-	struct msm_drm_private *priv = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
-
-	if (priv->kms_init)
-		component_del(&pdev->dev, &a3xx_ops);
-	else
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(pdev->dev.of_node, "amd,imageon") ||
+	    msm_gpu_no_components())
 		msm_gpu_remove(pdev, &a3xx_ops);
+	else
+		component_del(&pdev->dev, &a3xx_ops);
 }
 
 static void adreno_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
